          <TextScrollReveal
              nodeId="HVAL9wFKO"
              width="1fr"
              height="fit-content"
              maxWidth="1200px"
              text="Sometimes the vision arrives faster than the architecture required to hold it.
Every new possibility opens another direction. The product is evolving while its identity is still forming. Decisions about brand, market, technology, and business model are being made simultaneously—each shaping the others.
There is tremendous intelligence in what is emerging. But the whole has not yet found its form.
And sometimes the architecture already exists, but the coherence has begun to fracture.
Decisions that should take one conversation now take four. The same words mean different things across the leadership team. Direction holds in the room and breaks in execution. The work is undeniable, but the market doesn't quite see what you see. You are doing more, and getting less.
Different moments. The same underlying question:
What does this system require to move as one?               
This is where ARCMA's work begins.
